From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:40:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webservices: take the struct options that only concern
 reading without a FIXME.

Office writes structures described with WS_STRUCT_IGNORE_TRAILING_ELEMENT_CONTENT
and WS_STRUCT_IGNORE_UNHANDLED_ATTRIBUTES, and each of the 154 writes
as Word started said the options were not supported.  Both say what a
reader should pass over, and change nothing a writer writes.  The reader
already passes over attributes no field describes, which is what the
second asks for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit cc8233ad05415d943e7509e41c44df624cf1dce2)

diff --git a/dlls/webservices/reader.c b/dlls/webservices/reader.c
index 119fcc14cf7..91107200eab 100644
--- a/dlls/webservices/reader.c
+++ b/dlls/webservices/reader.c
@@ -6466,10 +6466,11 @@ static HRESULT read_type_struct( struct reader *reader, WS_TYPE_MAPPING mapping,
     char *buf;
 
     if (!desc) return E_INVALIDARG;
-    if (desc->structOptions & ~WS_STRUCT_IGNORE_TRAILING_ELEMENT_CONTENT)
+    /* attributes no field describes are passed over, which is what WS_STRUCT_IGNORE_UNHANDLED_ATTRIBUTES asks for */
+    if (desc->structOptions & ~(WS_STRUCT_IGNORE_TRAILING_ELEMENT_CONTENT | WS_STRUCT_IGNORE_UNHANDLED_ATTRIBUTES))
     {
         FIXME( "struct options %#lx not supported\n",
-               desc->structOptions & ~WS_STRUCT_IGNORE_TRAILING_ELEMENT_CONTENT );
+               desc->structOptions & ~(WS_STRUCT_IGNORE_TRAILING_ELEMENT_CONTENT | WS_STRUCT_IGNORE_UNHANDLED_ATTRIBUTES) );
     }
 
     switch (option)
diff --git a/dlls/webservices/writer.c b/dlls/webservices/writer.c
index 92a6ce30178..f4326a12b06 100644
--- a/dlls/webservices/writer.c
+++ b/dlls/webservices/writer.c
@@ -3883,7 +3883,9 @@ static HRESULT write_type_struct( struct writer *writer, WS_TYPE_MAPPING mapping
     HRESULT hr;
 
     if (!desc) return E_INVALIDARG;
-    if (desc->structOptions) FIXME( "struct options %#lx not supported\n", desc->structOptions );
+    /* what to ignore in what is read changes nothing in what is written */
+    if (desc->structOptions & ~(WS_STRUCT_IGNORE_TRAILING_ELEMENT_CONTENT | WS_STRUCT_IGNORE_UNHANDLED_ATTRIBUTES))
+        FIXME( "struct options %#lx not supported\n", desc->structOptions );
 
     if ((hr = get_value_ptr( option, value, size, desc->size, &ptr )) != S_OK) return hr;
     if (option == WS_WRITE_NILLABLE_POINTER && !ptr) return write_add_nil_attribute( writer );
